{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774300422,"nonce":"36Sg+if4oXCs4K68bLzoYZtGbEA=","message":"Implementation spec for demand-driven analysis execution:\n\n1. Add requested_outputs: set[str] | None = None to compute_dependency_results()\n   - When None: behave as today (compute all nodes in topological order)\n   - When provided: filter execution to only ancestors of requested outputs\n\n2. Ancestor filtering algorithm in compute_dependency_results():\n   a. After building graph and topological order, resolve requested_outputs to node_ids:\n      - Match against dependency_lookup keys (analysis names)\n      - Fall back to matching node_labels for custom dependencies\n   b. Collect ancestors: BFS/DFS from requested node_ids through graph edges (graph[node] gives dependencies of node, so follow those recursively)\n   c. Filter comp_order to only include ancestor node_ids + the requested nodes themselves\n   d. Also filter leaf_node_ids to only requested ones\n\n3. Thread the parameter through:\n   - perform_all_analyses(... requested_outputs=None) -\u003e compute_dependency_results()\n   - run_analyses(... requested_outputs=None) -\u003e perform_all_analyses()\n\n4. When requested_outputs is provided:\n   - Only nodes in the ancestor set are computed\n   - Only requested leaf analyses get figure generation\n   - analyses dict is filtered to requested keys before passing to downstream logic","files":null}]}